      "id": "import",
      "title": "Import",
      "members": [],
      "paragraphs": [
        "The lighting system: lights, materials and occluders in, a shaded frame out.",
        "```ts const lighting = new Lighting({ quality: 'lightmap', app, ambient: new Color(11, 16, 32) });",
        "scene.systems.add(lighting); lighting.add(player.addChild(new PointLight({ radius: 260 }))); lighting.occludeFrom(new PhysicsOccluder(world)); ```",
        "# What it owns",
        "The renderer and its GPU resources. Lights are scene nodes owned by the tree they hang in - registering one does not transfer ownership, and destroying a registered light unregisters it. Occluder sources and filters passed as `post` are the caller's too.",
        "# Ordering",
        "Register it with the registry that ticks AFTER the code moving the lights, so the frame it shades is the frame that was drawn. `app.systems` runs its update phase before the active scene's, so a system registered there sees lights the scene has not moved yet; `scene.systems` is usually what you want."
      ],
      "importLine": "import { Lighting } from '@codexo/exojs-lighting'",
      "sourceLink": null
